@startuml Preciazo_Identity_Access_States
title Preciazo - Sign-in Control States (AV2 - US06)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 60
state "Ready for Sign-in" as READY
state "Temporarily Blocked" as BLOCKED
state "Security Check Required" as CHECK
[*] --> READY : active registered account
READY -down-> BLOCKED : failures reach configured threshold
BLOCKED -down-> CHECK : now >= lockedUntil\n(derived on request)
CHECK --> READY : valid proof + correct password\nreset all sign-in controls
CHECK --> BLOCKED : valid proof + wrong password\nnew failure threshold reached
note right of READY
 Correct password: accepted decision; reset failures.
 Wrong password below threshold: remain READY and record failure.
end note
note right of BLOCKED
 Before expiry: remain BLOCKED, without extending the deadline.
 Expiry is evaluated on request, not by a scheduled event.
 Existing bearer tokens are not revoked by this sign-in block.
end note
note right of CHECK
 Missing/invalid proof: remain CHECK; no token.
 Valid proof + wrong password below threshold: remain CHECK.
 First valid-proof attempt after expiry starts a new failure window;
 further wrong passwords increment it, without restarting the window.
 A fresh proof is required for each new request until successful sign-in.
 Provider failure leaves controls unchanged and issues no token.
end note
note bottom of CHECK
 SUSPENDED / DEACTIVATED status denies sign-in independently.
 This diagram shows sign-in controls, not access-token lifecycle.
end note
@enduml
